sub create | Create a resource from a file or from stdin
sub expose | Take a replication controller, service, deployment or pod an
sub run | Run a particular image on the cluster
sub set | Set specific features on objects
sub explain | Get documentation for a resource
sub get | Display one or many resources
sub edit | Edit a resource on the server
sub delete | Delete resources by file names, stdin, resources and names,
sub rollout | Manage the rollout of a resource
sub scale | Set a new size for a deployment, replica set, or replication
sub autoscale | Auto-scale a deployment, replica set, stateful set, or repli
sub certificate | Modify certificate resources
sub cluster-info | Display cluster information
sub top | Display resource (CPU/memory) usage
sub cordon | Mark node as unschedulable
sub uncordon | Mark node as schedulable
sub drain | Drain node in preparation for maintenance
sub taint | Update the taints on one or more nodes
sub describe | Show details of a specific resource or group of resources
sub logs | Print the logs for a container in a pod
sub attach | Attach to a running container
sub exec | Execute a command in a container
sub port-forward | Forward one or more local ports to a pod
sub proxy | Run a proxy to the Kubernetes API server
sub cp | Copy files and directories to and from containers
sub auth | Inspect authorization
sub debug | Create debugging sessions for troubleshooting workloads and
sub events | List events
sub diff | Diff the live version against a would-be applied version
sub apply | Apply a configuration to a resource by file name or stdin
sub patch | Update fields of a resource
sub replace | Replace a resource by file name or stdin
sub wait | Wait for a specific condition on one or many resources
sub kustomize | Build a kustomization target from a directory or URL
sub label | Update the labels on a resource
sub annotate | Update the annotations on a resource
sub completion | Output shell completion code for the specified shell (bash,
sub api-resources | Print the supported API resources on the server
sub api-versions | Print the supported API versions on the server, in the form
sub config | Modify kubeconfig files
sub kuberc | Manage kuberc configuration files
sub plugin | Provides utilities for interacting with plugins
sub version | Print the client and server version information
